    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "It does this weird thing where it'll jump to the end of the file and show you a little warning if it doesn't find a custom text object, and worse is you can't `ctrl-o` back to position before you jumped. Is there a way to just show a warning and not jump if an object is not found?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It does this weird thing where it'll jump to the end of the file and show you a little warning if it doesn't find a custom text object, and worse is you can't <code class=\"notranslate\">ctrl-o</code> back to position before you jumped. Is there a way to just show a warning and not jump if an object is not found?</p>",
